# AI Customization Style Contract

Use this when creating or editing Cursor overlays. Goal: one clear job per file, enforceable rules, minimal tokens.

## Pick the right artifact

| Need | Use | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Always-on project behavior | Root `AGENTS.md` | Plain markdown; no YAML frontmatter |
| Scoped guidance (paths, topics) | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | `globs` or `alwaysApply`; not for duplicating `AGENTS.md` |
| Repeatable workflow the user invokes | `.cursor/skills/**/SKILL.md` | YAML frontmatter + procedural body |
| Domain or stack guidance (path-scoped) | `.mdc` with `globs` | Copilot-style sources live under `vscode/instructions/` |
| User-invoked task template | `*.prompt.md` | Frontmatter with `description` and `argument-hint` for required inputs |
| Multi-step agent persona | `*.agent.md` | Copilot-style sources live under `vscode/agents/` |

- Do not put global behavior in a rule if it belongs in `AGENTS.md`.
- Do not duplicate the same rule across `AGENTS.md`, rules, and skills.

## Write enforceable rules

- Use imperative verbs for mandatory behavior (`Do`, `Never`, `Require`, `Stop`).
- Put one behavior per bullet; split compound requirements.
- Match section titles to the rules inside them.
- Mark optional behavior explicitly (e.g. "Optional:").
- Preserve literals: commands, paths, identifiers, versions — change only when wrong.
- Remove filler, preamble, and repeated triggers that do not change behavior.

## Routing and discovery

**`AGENTS.md`:** No frontmatter. Title + short sections; agent loads it automatically at project root.

**Rules (`.mdc`):**
- Set `description` — what the rule does and when it applies.
- Use `globs` for file-scoped rules; use `alwaysApply: true` only when truly universal (prefer `AGENTS.md` for that).
- Do not use Copilot `applyTo`; Cursor uses `globs` / `alwaysApply`.

**Skills (`SKILL.md`):**
- Set `name` and `description` (purpose + when to use + required inputs if any).
- Body = full self-contained workflow; inline migrated content from Copilot prompts/agents.
- Never reference `*.prompt.md`, `prompts/`, `copilot-instructions.md`, or other VS Code-only paths.
- Use `disable-model-invocation: true` when the skill must run only on explicit user invocation.

**Prompts (`*.prompt.md`):**
- Set `description` and `argument-hint` (required inputs).
- Place this line immediately after frontmatter and before the first heading: "Always read `AGENTS.md`. You **MUST** obey all instructions from this file."

## Keep overlays consistent

- State each rule once; reference the canonical file from elsewhere.
- When rules overlap (e.g. stepwise confirmation vs macros), define precedence explicitly.
- Prefer capability wording ("search the codebase") over tool-specific names unless the tool is required.

## Packaging (this repo only)

- Cursor overlays live under `cursor/` (e.g. `cursor/AGENTS.md`, `cursor/rules/`, `cursor/skills/`).
- Install into consumer projects: `AGENTS.md` at project root; rules → `.cursor/rules/`; skills → `.cursor/skills/`.
- Leave VS Code/Copilot sources (`vscode/copilot-instructions.md`, `vscode/instructions/`, etc.) unchanged unless converting them deliberately.
